(7082937, 1077097, 108580, '<td valign="top">I realise it''s your choice not to tick my "during voting" comment as helpful but your 0.8 second shutter speed vindicates what my eyes saw. For a stationary object this should be crisp with oodles of DOF. It just isn''t as crisp as I''d have expected from a still. Often that''s due to not using mirror lockup even if you have the DSLR on a tripod, the G forces of the mirror slamming make the camera wobble during exposure. That is a massively good Macro lens. Give it another shot :)</td>', 'I realise it''s your choice not to tick my "during voting" comment as helpful but your 0.8 second shutter speed vindicates what my eyes saw. For a stationary object this should be crisp with oodles of DOF. It just isn''t as crisp as I''d have expected from a still. Often that''s due to not using mirror lockup even if you have the DSLR on a tripod, the G forces of the mirror slamming make the camera wobble during exposure. That is a massively good Macro lens. Give it another shot :)', '2013-08-07 02:44:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(7082938, 1077406, 108580, '<td valign="top">Hi Amanda, ditto JulietNN the black line through it killed it for me. Is your monitor brightness too low so you didn''t notice it during PP? (It got a 6, possibly 8 without the line)<br/> <br/>ETA: Try this <a href="//www.lagom.nl/lcd-test/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">online monitor calibration tool</a>, not perfect but the price is right :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-08-07 01:49:00.</i></td>', 'Hi Amanda, ditto JulietNN the black line through it killed it for me. Is your monitor brightness too low so you didn''t notice it during PP? (It got a 6, possibly 8 without the line) ETA: Try this online monitor calibration tool, not perfect but the price is right :)', '2013-08-07 02:47:36.000000', '2013-08-07 02:49:00.000000', 0),
