(7083263, 1077431, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SamPawley:</b></div><hr/><i> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1078346" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/130000-134999/130561/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1078346.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/130000-134999/130561/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1078346.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/130000-134999/130561/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1078346.jpg"/></a> <br/>Nautilus In Colour - I never entered this in Colour as I thought Black and White would enhance the Black on Black Theme...I was concerned if I entered the colour it would be too Blue for the Black on Black challenge. After the competition opened and I saw other Colour photos....well, I Kicked myself!<br/> <br/>I am still very happy with both Photos &amp; very greatful for all of your Comments </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>don''t kick yourself. you never would have ribboned with that much blue in the photo.</td>', 'Originally posted by SamPawley:  Nautilus In Colour - I never entered this in Colour as I thought Black and White would enhance the Black on Black Theme...I was concerned if I entered the colour it would be too Blue for the Black on Black challenge. After the competition opened and I saw other Colour photos....well, I Kicked myself! I am still very happy with both Photos & very greatful for all of your Comments   don''t kick yourself. you never would have ribboned with that much blue in the photo.', '2013-08-07 13:35:32.000000', NULL, 0),
