(7085468, 1077107, 51638, '<td valign="top">Really surprised this didn''t do much better. Perhaps voters punished you for the small splash of colour? FWIW I gave you an 8.</td>', 'Really surprised this didn''t do much better. Perhaps voters punished you for the small splash of colour? FWIW I gave you an 8.', '2013-08-11 21:55:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7087649, 1077431, 130561, '<td valign="top">Not happy that this was removed!!! i did not move, remove or duplicate any element of my photograph!<br/>All i did was darken the background, sharpen the image and make it Black and White.<br/> <br/>My second ever entry and I am still happy that people liked my photo enough to make it 3rd Place. <br/> <br/>Whatever DPC!</td>', 'Not happy that this was removed!!! i did not move, remove or duplicate any element of my photograph!All i did was darken the background, sharpen the image and make it Black and White. My second ever entry and I am still happy that people liked my photo enough to make it 3rd Place.  Whatever DPC!', '2013-08-15 05:49:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7089048, 1077431, 96751, '<td valign="top">What a pity, Sam. Don''t be disheartened. Just about everyone around here has been DQ''d at some point. One of the hardest things to learn on DPC is the editing rules, and how far you can push the envelop on each before it''s no longer "legal". Just remember that a DQ has nothing to do with the quality of the image, which in this case is splendid.</td>', 'What a pity, Sam. Don''t be disheartened. Just about everyone around here has been DQ''d at some point. One of the hardest things to learn on DPC is the editing rules, and how far you can push the envelop on each before it''s no longer "legal". Just remember that a DQ has nothing to do with the quality of the image, which in this case is splendid.', '2013-08-18 12:25:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7089049, 1077431, 61396, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SamPawley:</b></div><hr/><i> Not happy that this was removed!!! i did not move, remove or duplicate any element of my photograph!<br/>All i did was darken the background, sharpen the image and make it Black and White.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Maybe the background was darkened so it lost any details it had initially? It is probably no consolation, but an entry of mine was DQ''ed for a similar reason (and I can''t claim being new around here).<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1049164" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1689/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1049164.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1689/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1049164.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1689/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1049164.jpg"/></a> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SamPawley:</b></div><hr/><i>My second ever entry and I am still happy that people liked my photo enough to make it 3rd Place. <br/> <br/>Whatever DPC! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>That''s the spirit!<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by SamPawley: Not happy that this was removed!!! i did not move, remove or duplicate any element of my photograph!All i did was darken the background, sharpen the image and make it Black and White. Maybe the background was darkened so it lost any details it had initially? It is probably no consolation, but an entry of mine was DQ''ed for a similar reason (and I can''t claim being new around here). Originally posted by SamPawley:My second ever entry and I am still happy that people liked my photo enough to make it 3rd Place.  Whatever DPC!  That''s the spirit!', '2013-08-18 12:27:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(7089076, 1077431, 114225, '<td valign="top">You made the right choice with B&amp;W. It''s easily 1000x more powerful and striking than the color version.<br/> <br/>Too bad for the DQ. This is one of those rules that has tripped up many people. Don''t fret, if you are getting a ribbon on your second entry, more are soon to follow.</td>', 'You made the right choice with B&W. It''s easily 1000x more powerful and striking than the color version. Too bad for the DQ. This is one of those rules that has tripped up many people. Don''t fret, if you are getting a ribbon on your second entry, more are soon to follow.', '2013-08-18 14:43:35.000000', NULL, 0),
